                        ],
                        "form": "paeans"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "fcedd21c-c745-4020-97fa-d9424c59a98e",
                        "entry_id": "b7f64592-f01d-3233-8cbb-c4343e91bcf2",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "paeaning"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "138e5557-6fcd-449c-9228-3648b4b762fb",
                        "entry_id": "b7f64592-f01d-3233-8cbb-c4343e91bcf2",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "paeaned"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "66ced0be-6e00-48e8-b21d-f4e3bb151ac8",
                        "entry_id": "b7f64592-f01d-3233-8cbb-c4343e91bcf2",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "paeaned"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6cec08fa-e0b5-33e6-b67b-b7dcc35bc11b",
                        "entry_id": "b7f64592-f01d-3233-8cbb-c4343e91bcf2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To sing a paean; to praise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d55274d1-3d6c-4036-a85c-9c511546aeac",
                                "sense_id": "6cec08fa-e0b5-33e6-b67b-b7dcc35bc11b",
                                "text": "Then let the pæaned hymn aspire, / Nor longer court unholy gloom; / Let happier music wake thy lyre, / Than haunts the precincts of the tomb."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "390f20f5-875c-42e9-97c2-e2c3aa0ac82e",
                                "sense_id": "6cec08fa-e0b5-33e6-b67b-b7dcc35bc11b",
                                "text": "Solemn, \"as it were a pause in nature,\" was his [George Washington's] transit to eternity; thronged by the shades of heroes, his approach to the confines of bliss; pæaned by the songs of angels, his journey beyond the stars!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "340f3466-6960-481f-8fa2-0aff8c140d42",
                                "sense_id": "6cec08fa-e0b5-33e6-b67b-b7dcc35bc11b",
                                "text": "What harbinger victorious tidings brings, / And yonder soars on golden wings? / Beams on the solar god her bright undazzled eyes, / Proclaims with pæaning trump some hero to the skies!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1c64b7e-bcb8-4b8e-8dee-45f2ac84eac5",
                                "sense_id": "6cec08fa-e0b5-33e6-b67b-b7dcc35bc11b",
                                "text": "Yea, with gladness did they pæan, bowing low before my car, / In my ears their homage echoed from the sunrise to the star."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "583bf2cd-e914-4519-8ad6-a7d2773964bf",
                                "sense_id": "6cec08fa-e0b5-33e6-b67b-b7dcc35bc11b",
                                "text": "Spring is the season of Nature's most lavish output—why not the publisher's also? Some may object that the output of the publisher does not resemble that of Nature; but this criticism seems to us to be trivial. The simple fact that Nature and the publisher are working together means everything. And therefore we are paeaning our paeans of literary joy. We celebrate books. We celebrate literary people. We hail authors and authoresses."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
